# Multi-module build: the single, process-global MCP server must report its status
# once — not once per aggregated subproject. `mcpStatus` on the root should print a
# single "running at ..." line. checkStatusNoAggregate asserts the mechanism
# (mcpStatus/aggregate = false) that guarantees this.
> mcpStatus
> checkStatusNoAggregate

# Compile all aggregated modules, then query through the real MCP handlers while
# the root is active. Both module-only symbols should be visible from the root.
> compile
> checkMultiModuleSymbols
